@startuml
package "Agent" {
  package "AutoConfiguration" {
    class ApAutoConfigurationTask
  }

  package "Tasks" {
    class TrafficSeparationTask
  }

  package "TrafficSeparation" {
    class TrafficSeparationManager
    abstract class PortPlumbing
    class TrunkPortPlumbing8021q
    class AccessPortPlumbing8021q
    struct sTrunkPort
    struct sAccessPort
    struct sTrafficSeparationConfig
  }

  class AgentDB
  class slave_thread
  class TaskPool
  class broker_client
  class BPL_CFG
  class network_utils
}

ApAutoConfigurationTask --> AgentDB : read TS policy and BSS role
ApAutoConfigurationTask --> slave_thread : task_pool_try_send_event(TS_ENABLE)\nafter radios configured or policy update\ntask_pool_try_send_event(TS_NEW_FH_IFACE)\non AP_ENABLED for pure FH BSS
ApAutoConfigurationTask --> slave_thread : task_pool_try_send_event(TS_CLEAR_WDS_IFACE / TS_NEW_WDS_IFACE)\non AP_ENABLED disallow-flag change
slave_thread --> AgentDB : read boot-time profile\naudit VAP snapshots\ntrack client WDS iface state
slave_thread --> TaskPool : add_task(TrafficSeparationTask)\nwhen TS is supported
slave_thread --> TaskPool : try_send_event(TS_ENABLE)\ntry_send_event(TS_NEW_FH_IFACE / TS_CLEAR_FH_IFACE)\nfrom AP disable or VAP snapshot transitions\ntry_send_event(TS_NEW_WDS_IFACE / TS_CLEAR_WDS_IFACE)\nfrom WDS notifications, association replacement,\nand disconnect cleanup
slave_thread --> TaskPool : try_send_event(TS_CLEAR_WDS_IFACE / TS_NEW_WDS_IFACE)\nfrom VAPS_LIST_UPDATE disallow-flag changes
slave_thread --> slave_thread : cache WDS notifications until\nprocess_client_association()
TaskPool --> TrafficSeparationTask : handle_event() only when task exists

TrafficSeparationTask --> AgentDB : read TS policy, persistent trunk inventory,\ncurrent runtime BSS and client state\nmatch exact WDS iface to active bBSS
TrafficSeparationTask --> BPL_CFG : read private/guest bridge names
TrafficSeparationTask --> broker_client : configure_primary_vlan_id()\nconfigure_interfaces()
TrafficSeparationTask --> TrafficSeparationManager : clear_policies()\nconfigure(cfg)\nadd_trunk_port(trunk)\nremove_trunk_port(iface_name)\nadd_access_port(access)\nremove_access_port(iface_name)\napply_policies()
TrafficSeparationTask --> slave_thread

TrafficSeparationManager --> PortPlumbing : apply(cfg)\nclear()
PortPlumbing <|-- TrunkPortPlumbing8021q
PortPlumbing <|-- AccessPortPlumbing8021q

TrunkPortPlumbing8021q --> network_utils : create_vlan_interface()\nlinux_add_iface_to_bridge()\nset_interface_state()
AccessPortPlumbing8021q --> network_utils : linux_iface_exists()\nset_vlan_packet_filter()

note bottom of TrafficSeparationTask
  TS_ENABLE stays on the debounced apply path.
  work() runs reset() for policy refresh and
  bounded WDS retries after the settle delay.

  reset() refreshes config plus persistent DB-owned
  trunks and preserves event-managed FH and WDS
  ownership.

  Pure-FH and exact-WDS add/remove are event-driven.
  WDS add does not sleep inside handle_event();
  readiness retry stays on the deferred work path.

  Policy disable currently reaches cleanup through
  TS_ENABLE plus primary_vlan_id=0. TS_CLEAR exists for
  explicit runtime cleanup but is not the normal policy
  disable producer in the current tree.
end note

@enduml
